  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 135 AM CDT Sun Aug 2 2026\n\nThe mid-level pattern over the CONUS through mid to late next week \nfeatures troughing from the Ohio Valley towards the Atlantic \ncoastline while ridging over the Desert Southwest elongates and \nstretches across Texas. This will result in a seasonably hot and \nrain free pattern across our local region. Daytime highs range in \nthe mid 90s to near 100 degrees and overnight lows in the mid to \nupper 70s. Low-level dew points and cloud cover gradually creep \nupwards, especially along and east of the I-35 corridor, with a \nslight uptick in the onshore flow coming from the gulf. Late week \ninto the start of the weekend may see isolated sea breeze activity \nacross the CRP/HGX CWAs that could approach our far southeastern \nmost counties, like Lavaca County, elsewhere rain free conditions \nshould prevail.",
